# ...except the shared template itself -- .env.* above was accidentally
# excluding .env.example too, so it had NEVER actually been committed
# (confirmed via `git log --all -- .env.example`: empty history). That
# silently defeated its whole purpose as the "copy this file to .env"
# onboarding starting point RUNBOOK.md and this project's own docs assume
# exists in the repo. Found while adding ADP-SPEC-044's env vars to it.
!.env.example

# Keep generated schema committed (it IS a source artifact per ART-II)
# generated/architecture-description.schema.json  ← NOT ignored

